DUPLICATE DOCUMENT HANDLING:

The current index allows duplicate doc_ids. Design decision needed:

OPTION A: Reject duplicates (return error)
```rust
pub fn add_entry(&mut self, entry: TwoTierEntry) -> SearchResult<()> {
    if self.doc_ids.contains(&entry.doc_id) {
        return Err(SearchError::DuplicateDocument(entry.doc_id));
    }
    // ... existing add logic
}
```

OPTION B: Update existing (replace old embedding)
```rust
pub fn add_or_update_entry(&mut self, entry: TwoTierEntry) -> SearchResult<()> {
    if let Some(idx) = self.doc_ids.iter().position(|&id| id == entry.doc_id) {
        // Update in place
        let start = idx * self.config.fast_dimension;
        self.fast_embeddings[start..start + self.config.fast_dimension]
            .copy_from_slice(&entry.fast_embedding);
        // ... similar for quality
        return Ok(());
    }
    // ... existing add logic for new doc
}
```

OPTION C: Allow duplicates (current behavior) - NOT RECOMMENDED

RECOMMENDATION: Option B (update existing) to handle message edits gracefully.

