- A way to assert on tracing events without brittle string matching.

Without a shared helpers crate we'll duplicate all of this 10+ times
and drift over time. Create the crate ONCE, reuse it.

## Deliverable

New workspace crate: `crates/mcp-agent-mail-test-helpers`.

Public API:

```
pub mod shim_git {
    pub struct ShimBehavior {
        pub version_output: String,        // what `--version` prints
        pub exit_codes: Vec<ExitSpec>,     // sequence: first call, second, etc.
        pub delay_ms: u64,                 // per-call delay
        pub side_effect: Option<PathBuf>,  // marker file to touch per call
    }
    pub fn build_shim(dir: &Path, behavior: ShimBehavior) -> PathBuf;
    pub enum ExitSpec {
        Ok, Exit(i32), Segfault, Bus, TimeoutNever,
    }
}

pub mod repo {
    pub fn empty() -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_commits(n: usize) -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_orphan_stash() -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_dangling_branch() -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_worktree(name: &str) -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_bare() -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_unicode_paths() -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_long_paths() -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_submodule() -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn with_gitignore(entries: &[&str]) -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    pub fn corrupt_config() -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    // Composable builder:
    pub struct RepoBuilder { ... }
    impl RepoBuilder {
        pub fn new() -> Self;
        pub fn commit(self, content: &str) -> Self;
        pub fn stash(self, content: &str) -> Self;
        pub fn orphan_stash(self) -> Self;   // stash then rm blob
        pub fn build(self) -> (TempDir, PathBuf);
    }
}

pub mod metrics {
    pub fn reset_all();
    pub fn snapshot() -> MetricsSnapshot;
    pub struct MetricsSnapshot { ... }
    impl MetricsSnapshot {
        pub fn counter(&self, name: &str) -> u64;
        pub fn histogram(&self, name: &str) -> Histogram;
        pub fn delta(&self, other: &Self) -> Self;
    }
}

pub mod tracing_assertions {
    pub fn capture_span<F: FnOnce()>(target: &str, level: Level, f: F) -> Vec<TracingEvent>;
    pub struct TracingEvent {
        pub target: String,
        pub level: Level,
        pub fields: HashMap<String, Value>,
    }
    pub fn assert_event_with_field(events: &[TracingEvent], name: &str, key: &str, val: &Value);
}

pub mod process {
    pub fn spawn_test_binary(crate_name: &str, bin_name: &str, args: &[&str]) -> Child;
    pub fn wait_for_port(port: u16, timeout: Duration) -> Result<()>;
}
```

### Dependencies

- Only used by `dev-dependencies` of other crates.
- Itself depends on: tempfile, git2, regex, serde_json, tracing,
  tracing-test.
- No new external deps beyond what the workspace already uses.

### Safety

- Every RepoBuilder / ShimBuilder returns the TempDir handle so the
  caller owns lifetime. Guards against accidental dangling tempdirs.
- Shim binaries built into the tempdir (not in global target/), so
  they clean up with the test.
- process::spawn_test_binary catches zombie children via a Drop
  impl that waits (with a 5s timeout, SIGKILL after).

### Migration plan

- After G6 ships:
    - Each Track-C test file that currently has inline fixture code
      migrates to use the helpers (mechanical edit; each ~20 lines
      shorter).
    - New tests (A5, E1, E2, etc.) write against the helpers from
      day one.

### Tests of the helpers crate itself

- tests/test_shim_git_builder.rs:
  - Build each ExitSpec variant.
  - Invoke it.
  - Assert observed behavior matches the spec.
- tests/test_repo_builder.rs:
  - Build each preset repo variant.
  - Walk with libgit2 to verify expected structure.
- tests/test_metrics_snapshot.rs:
  - Reset; increment counters; snapshot; assert values.
  - Delta between two snapshots yields expected diffs.
- tests/test_tracing_capture.rs:
  - Emit events inside capture_span.
  - Assert captured events match expectations.

### Logging

- Helpers are test infra; they log via tracing at DEBUG only so
  they don't pollute test output unless `-- --nocapture` + RUST_LOG.
- Panics include descriptive messages with the input that caused
  the failure (e.g., 'build_shim: behavior.exit_codes.len() == 0 is
  invalid').

